     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<br><br>This morning workflowr was published on <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/package=workflowr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/package%3Dworkflowr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793246925120000&amp;usg=AOvVaw13Cpkzr5-1h02vpxuMp_Op\">CRAN</a>. You can now easily install workflowr with install.packages:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">install</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;workflowr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>And please remember to send any feature requests or feedback to the <a href=\"https://github.com/jdblischak/workflowr/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jdblischak/workflowr/issues&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793246925120000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3MfT2yGiZvuBJdNebtFTL9\">GitHub Issues</a>. The new &quot;reproducibility report&quot; is still in development, so you can help shape its features and appearance.<br><br>John</div>"
